      en: ["Himeji in Hyogo Prefecture is best known for its brilliant white Himeji Castle, a UNESCO World Heritage site. It is the largest and best-preserved feudal fortress in the country, often called the 'White Heron Castle'.", "Located within the island nation of Japan in the North Pacific.", "Plays a role in the local identity of the region.", "Known for its scenic or cultural significance.", "Documented in local and regional studies."],
