      en: ["Fukui on the west coast is historically significant for the Sengoku-period excavation site of the Asakura clan. In modern times, the city is most famous for the nearby Prefectural Dinosaur Museum, one of the world's leading paleontological institutions.", "Located within the island nation of Japan in the North Pacific.", "Plays a role in the local identity of the region.", "Known for its scenic or cultural significance.", "Documented in local and regional studies."],
